Creating the function alone will not execute it.
Example:
def show_message():
    print("Welcome to Python")
There is no output yet.

We need to call the function.
def show_message():
    print("Welcome to Python")

show_message()
Output
Welcome to Python

Understand the flow:
def show_message():
        ↓
Function Created


show_message()
        ↓
Function Called
        ↓
Code Executes
